WEBVTT

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.650
When I open my photo book, I see different sides of me. {purichou...}

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.420
Laughing, {warattari}

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.200
or playing it cool, in all the pictures. {sumashitari de...}

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.930
I don't wanna say, "what's with all these characters?" But... {nani kore...}

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.640
Isn't this too much fun? {arisugi...}

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.220
For real? {maji...}

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.430
I mean, thanks! {tte yuu ka...}

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.760
Even if I lose my way,  {maigo ni...}

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.370
my heart's egg {kokoro no...}

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.140
will be all right. Come back {daijoubu...}

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.830
to me! {modotteoide}

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.610
Hey, when we're together... {kimi to...}

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.330
Hop, step, jump!

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.940
Because you're here... {kimi ga...}

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.590
Drew, draw, drawn!

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.460
I'm always with you...  {kimi to...}

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.180
Chip, syrup, whip!

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.860
One more time,  {mou ichido...}

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.470
unlock my heart! {kokoro...}

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.240
I love you.  {daisuki yo}

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.700
All of you.  {minna}

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.590
I want to be next to you. {soba ni...}

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.900
Okay? {ne...}

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.050
Love ya! {suki yo}

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:55.470
There's no end in sight.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.270
Um, it's kind of sudden, but summer vacation is almost over, isn't it?

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.500
Isn't it?

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.800
There's not much time left to have fun.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.100
Although, she'll probably be doing homework the whole time.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:07.840
Yes!

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:10.780
We've got Japanese, Mathematics, Science, Social Studies,

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:13.930
an independent research project, and a book report!

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:18.060
Silence! If I can't concentrate, I'll never make progress!

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.880
Uh-oh, Amu-chan got mad!

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.020
An angry outburst, even though she's the heroine!

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.490
An angry outburst!

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:28.400
Hey!

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.660
Man, they just run and hide in their eggs right away.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.120
But now I can concentrate on my homework.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.100
Okay let's get all this stuff out of the way-

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.970
Sis, Sis, phone for you!

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.920
It's from an old lady I dunno!

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:43.460
Old la-

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.560
Old lady?

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.740
I'm Utau's Manager?

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.740
Episode 47

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.720
Sanjo Productions

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.710
You want me to be Utau's Manager?!

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:57.710
Yeah,

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.170
I'd like you to take my place, just for today.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.640
Of all the times for me to get sick...

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.780
So the old lady was Kairi-kun's older sister.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.030
Did you say something?

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.310
Nope, nothing.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.820
Are you okay?

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.280
Sorry about this.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.460
It's such a crucial time for us to promote the new song, and I...

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:23.150
Then that's all the more reason...

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.350
I mean, me? The manager?

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.450
You're not fit to be my manager, agreed?

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.660
More like an attendant, or errand boy.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:36.240
I'm so glad to see you again, Amu-chan.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.410
El!

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.480
And I also welcome the Children's Trio, as a bonus.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.380
Children's Trio?

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:42.960
As a bonus?

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.370
It's about time to go.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.030
Will you really be okay?

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.220
I'm just going to the same old TV station I always go to.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.470
All right. Sorry about this.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:54.780
But it's really impossible for me to be the manager!

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:57.660
It's not like I planned to bring you along.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.640
What's that? Well, it's not like I want to work for you anyway!

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.490
Fine, no problem. I'll just go by myself.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.170
I knew it, I should go-

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.200
Sanjo-san!

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.020
Amu-chan, you don't have time to worry.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.560
People are in trouble!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.980
I suppose so. I guess I don't have a choice.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.100
Yeah, let's do it!

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.050
Showbusiness...

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.720
This might be fun!

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.800
What are you standing around for? We're leaving.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.820
If you're comin', hurry up!

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.000
Those two are so not cute.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.120
This is the first time we've been on the subway!

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.890
I am so excited!

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:42.010
I always assumed you were the type who'd take a taxi or have someone pick them up in a car, Utau.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.380
I never thought you'd take something like the subway.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.340
It's always in a tunnel.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:51.730
Just like a mole!

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:52.630
You bunch of babies! {note, the usage of "gaki" here is specifically to make fun of their lack of life experience, so using "brats" or "squirts" doesn't work}

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:58.750
Do you think I can really be your manager?

00:04:58.750 --> 00:05:00.590
No problem!

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:06.730
No use worrying! As long as you have this super special item, no problem will be unsolvable!

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.520
Super special item?

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.100
Glasses!

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.190
Now Amu-chan can be a POSitive managER!

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.380
To abbreviate, a POSER! {this is a partial rewrite to attempt to recreate the joke in english, the original joke "bi-mane" means "someone pretending to be effective"}

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.930
Poser?

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:19.960
But I guess these are pretty cool. They've got the <i>look.</i>

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.060
Yep, very effective!

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:21.890
Super skilled!

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.650
Okay, I wouldn't go that far.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.660
What's that girl going on about?

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:26.680
Well, that might be true, I guess.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.770
It has been hot out recently, so...

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.780
Oh, quit it!

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:30.020
Hey, stop staring at her.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.060
Idiot.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.020
Normal people can't see Guardian Characters, remember.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.810
We've arrived at the TV station!

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:44.310
Yes, got it. Understood.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.220
Okay, thanks a lot then.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.670
Good morning.

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:51.280
Thanks for having me today.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.250
Ah, just who I wanted to see.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.270
Utau-chan, could we please cancel that job today?

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.520
What do you mean, cancel?

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.640
You got bumped.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.190
Sorry 'bout this.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.640
Hold on a second!

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.280
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.720
T-Trouble already?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:12.940
It's a lot of things. You know, grown-up stuff.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.360
Explain it to me.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:16.610
Where's Sanjo-san?

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:17.970
My manager for today is

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.310
this girl.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.700
N-Nice to meet you.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:23.410
Amu-chan, you're too jittery.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.810
Relax!

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:28.080
I can't really talk about it if Sanjo-san isn't here.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.850
Anyway, that's it for today.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.660
Wait!

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.770
Hey there, if it isn't Utau-chan!

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:40.560
It's us, DARTS!

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.150
Who?

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.890
It's one of Easter's idol units.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.670
They're Sho, Gaku, and Seito.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:51.880
I think I've heard of them before.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.610
Looks like you're having a rough time after leaving the company.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:55.860
You haven't had any work, right?

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:02.540
And you haven't sung on any of the music shows, so we've been worried.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:07.270
But if you're here in the studio, that must mean you got some work! Thank goodness.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:11.150
Utau!

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.990
You want a picture, huh?

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.620
No need to restrain yourself.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.140
That's right!

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.740
Utau, wait!

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:22.810
Huh?

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.040
Wait up, Utau!

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.170
What's going on?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:30.030
The job was cancelled?

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:34.220
You were right there when they said they don't need someone like me.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.080
That's all.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:39.750
Don't need you? But you're a super popular singer.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.020
Are you making fun of her?

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:46.740
I'm not popular at all right now.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:49.230
I haven't had any radio or TV appearances.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.400
Why?

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.040
Because she left Easter.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.450
Really? Just because you quit?

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:00.950
They <i>are</i> the biggest player in the entertainment world. They're just retaliating.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:04.390
The fact that I decided to up and quit on my own makes it worse.

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:06.060
It's the worst impression you can make on the world.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:10.150
Did you really not know?

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:10.850
No.

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:13.650
"Selfish." "Audacious." "Mistake."

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:19.180
Everyone's saying these bad things all over the place, turning Utau-chan completely into the villain.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.510
Villain?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:32.200
You ungrateful traitor!

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:34.450
Brazen, selfish, and rude!

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.730
Get out of our town!

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:38.120
Yeah, yeah, out with you!

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.010
That's scary!

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.270
We haven't had any work lately.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:52.210
I'm sure her manager went to a lot of trouble to get the job we had today.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:56.150
So that's why we took the subway like regular people.

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:59.660
I see. We should ask Sanjo-san what to do.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.530
Don't butt in!

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.500
But...

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.960
She doesn't want to worry her manager when she's sick.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.100
It's her sense of compassion.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.270
El!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:15.390
I wonder if Utau handled it okay.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:18.770
It's no use, whenever I feel this sick my mind starts to... {a bit non literal}

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.000
Ah, I'm even hallucinating about Yuu.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.060
Wait, he's real?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.680
A bit careless, aren't we?

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.010
The door was unlocked.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.480
So how was Hinamori-san?

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:39.270
I asked her to help out based on your recommendation,

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.250
but do you really think that's okay?

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.920
I think she'd be better than I would be, if that's saying anything.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.700
But don't go asking me.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:50.220
My poor useless body! Just when Utau needs me, I...

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.170
At your age, you shouldn't push your-

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:55.360
Y-You seem pretty healthy to me.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:04.210
She finally has a new song, but hasn't sung it at all.

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.900
I feel like I have to do something.

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:10.570
Utau had a good reason for leaving Easter, though.

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:14.220
Because they made all those X Eggs and X Characters.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.880
Normal folks ain't gonna understand that!

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:21.190
I'm a singer whose success was only because of Easter's work.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:24.210
That's how the world sees me.

00:10:24.210 --> 00:10:29.450
The CD sales, the media exposure, my status as a diva...

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:32.210
That was all Easter's doing.

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:35.090
No, that's not true.

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.410
I've always thought

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.880
that your songs were really wonderful.

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:44.410
Until now, I've had my place as a singer handed to me.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:48.820
Which is why I'm going to find my own place to sing,

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:51.500
using only my own power!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:52.750
Utau.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.020
All right! I'm going to get you some work!

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:58.270
Huh? What are you saying?

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.980
Let's find a gig today, Utau!

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:02.590
Okay?

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.020
What are you suddenly going on about?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:08.130
Were you moved by my story or something?

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:10.020
N-Not a chance!

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.090
It's a manager's duty, right?

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:15.640
You look weird. Not like I care, though.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:19.140
Anyway, let's ask that guy one more time!

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:25.850
Hurry up! If you keep standing around, I'll leave you behind!

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.280
Sheesh.

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.040
I just don't get her.

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:45.810
Please!

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.100
Let Utau sing!

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.770
You're persistent, aren't you?

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.500
No matter how many times you ask...

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:54.230
Maybe so, but I'm begging you!

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.280
Amu.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:00.380
Jerk!

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.260
Jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk!

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:03.840
Let's go to a different TV station.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:05.810
Or a radio station, or even a publisher.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.450
You know where they are, right?

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:10.220
We're totally gonna get you a job!

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.720
Yeah!

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.270
Please, please!

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:26.030
Even so, please!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.100
Okay!

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:38.650
Please!

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.520
Let Utau sing!

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.220
Now matter how many times you ask, what's impossible remains impossible.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.770
Please!

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:50.400
Utau.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.030
I told you, right?

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:56.690
I'm going to find my place to sing with my own power.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:59.600
Besides that, I'd rather not be in your debt.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.810
I'm not doing this expecting anything in return.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:07.060
Please let her sing!

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.060
Please let me sing!

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.630
I'm sorry, but I don't have the authority to let anyone sing.

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:12.690
Sorry.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:17.390
Oh? Aren't those two children...

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:26.980
Hoshina Utau. She's been completely worthless lately.

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:28.600
Her career's so over.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.100
I'm sure those kids will be okay.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:34.080
After all, they have guardian spirits...

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.760
I mean, Guardian Characters with them!

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:38.860
What's that?

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:40.300
Let's just take it as it is.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.680
That's our Madame!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.580
You've got that right!

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.060
Who do you think I am?

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:49.100
I'm Saeki Nobuko!

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.690
Give Utau a chance!

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:54.000
A chance!

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.110
A chance!

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:57.020
A chance!

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.020
I wonder why no one will let you sing.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:03.270
It's because my song hasn't reached anyone.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.390
Utau.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.600
The day's not done yet.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:10.180
Let's go to the next one!

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:10.970
Of course!

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:16.710
The feeling of wanting to sing is growing stronger and stronger.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:22.470
Sanjo Productions

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:24.590
What are you doing?

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.060
Utau just won't pick up her phone.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.730
It's because she's in the middle of work.

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:32.770
I heard from the program's producer.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.900
The job was cancelled.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:36.430
Because of Easter?

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:39.020
Maybe it's because she was so shocked that...

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:43.380
You made rice porridge for me?

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:46.310
The prepackaged kind, I see.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.390
It was harder to make than it looks.

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:51.270
I wish she'd been here at a time like this.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.180
Please eat up!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.270
Who's this "she?"

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.100
Uh, well...

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:06.170
Even the prepackaged kind is good when someone makes it for you.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:08.550
Doesn't it?

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.850
Ah, in the end, we couldn't find any work.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:21.930
I wasn't able to find a place to sing.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:29.790
Everyone looks really tired.

00:15:31.810 --> 00:15:34.300
Hey, would you buy me some juice?

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.500
Huh?

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.020
You're my manager, right?

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:38.810
Understood.

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:42.140
You guys go, too!

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.080
It's hard being the manager.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:46.850
You can say that again.

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:56.350
...heartful song. I'll sing forever

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.850
Utau's new song?

00:15:56.350 --> 00:16:03.990
and wish for it to reach you.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:02.350
What a sweet, pretty melody. It's such a kind song.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.140
We still have some left.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.640
Have you seen Ikuto?

00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:16.420
Where did that come from?

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.310
Well?

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:20.220
I haven't seen him at all.

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:23.020
That day was the last time.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:26.370
Really?

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:27.400
Really.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.200
And how about you?

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:31.280
Is Ikuto doing okay?

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:33.720
I haven't heard from him since that night.

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:39.390
So what's the relationship between Ikuto and Easter, anyway?

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:42.390
What's the wish that you're trying to grant for him?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:48.000
I guess I can't ask any more than that, can I?

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.190
The new song is Ikuto's.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:56.370
It's a song he wrote for me a long time ago, and I added lyrics to it.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.100
I see.

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:05.740
That's why it's so sweet and pretty, but has such a sorrowful melody.

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:07.990
Amu-chan!

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:09.060
What is it, Ran?

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:09.930
Look!

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.530
An X Egg!

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:16.680
That X Egg was born from someone's tired heart.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:18.270
Let's go!

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:19.000
Right!

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.310
Just leave it alone!

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.550
For that egg to become an X Egg so easily,

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:27.010
the owner must've thrown it away themselves.

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:30.640
I disagree. I can't just leave it alone.

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:41.030
Let's go, Amu-chan!

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:41.640
Okay!

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:45.780
My heart:

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:46.560
Unlock!

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.370
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.160
Hey, Utau!

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:12.100
Again?

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:20.010
Utau-chan!

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:22.820
How can they just throw away who they want to be so easily?

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:25.120
I've been working hard this whole time.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.120
Even now, I'm still trying my best!

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:30.460
Who cares about those people's eggs?

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.910
I understand how you feel, Utau-chan,

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:37.350
but those people need your song!

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:42.520
My unneccessary song

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:46.970
is actually needed by those X Characters?

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:50.040
How ironic.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:52.930
Just leave those X Characters be. Who cares about 'em?

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:53.960
I'll do it.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:55.640
I...

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:58.220
I want to sing!

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:00.840
My heart:

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.770
Unlock!

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:20.470
Character Transformation: Seraphic Charm!

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:26.560
Concrete Jungle!

00:19:33.250 --> 00:19:35.730
Angel Cradle!

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:02.080
Yup, your singing really is amazing!

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.410
Was it over here?

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:06.020
Yeah, I thought I heard Utau's voice.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:09.700
What is that girl doing?

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:10.680
Uh-oh.

00:20:16.970 --> 00:20:19.270
Open Heart!

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:33.980
You did it, Amu-chan!

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:36.420
Though it was cut a bit short today.

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:43.740
What's this?

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:45.390
Utau is...

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:56.150
Give birth to a new me,

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:54.600
Isn't that Hoshina Utau?

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.500
Why is she singing at a place like this?

00:20:56.150 --> 00:21:06.000
have courage, don't be embarrassed.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:01.370
Still, she's amazing.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:06.020
Yeah, this song is great. I think I'm going to cry!

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:13.390
My heartful song, my heartful song.

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.390
I send you my song.

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:28.240
I'll sing forever, and wish for it to reach you.

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:18.970
Wow, she made her own place to sing!

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:34.150
What is she doing here?

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:37.020
She's not getting a single cent from this. {lit: yen, but here an americanization is appropriate}

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:52.510
One day, I hope you'll show me your true smile.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.770
Oh well, whatever.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:54.890
Ah, what am I going to do?!

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:59.630
Tomorrow's the start of the new term, and I didn't do any of my homework!

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.600
Is there anything I can use in these notes? I don't get it!

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:05.650
We've got Japanese, Mathematics, Science, Social Studies,

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:08.600
an independent research project, and a book report!

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.090
I told you not to sing!

00:22:10.090 --> 00:22:12.190
Amu-chan got mad!

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:13.660
Run away, run away!

00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:15.540
While we still can!

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:19.130
What am I going to do about my homework?

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:42.730
There's no limit to the dreams we wild things can see.  {abarenbou...}

00:22:42.730 --> 00:22:43.870
(Yeah, yeah, yeah.)

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:47.080
If we're born with 100% possibilities,  {kanouseo...}

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.030
then let's keep livin' at 100%. {hyakupa...}

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:54.870
Let's cry and laugh, {naritari...}

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:58.490
and meet all kinds of people.  {ironna...}

00:22:58.490 --> 00:23:02.030
Let's discover what's precious, {daiji na}

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:05.040
and even lose it. {nakushitari}

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:05.790
(But don't worry.) {hai donmai...}

00:23:05.790 --> 00:23:09.410
We've just gotta keep on runnin', {gan gan...}

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:12.200
because that way's the most fun, you see.  {sono hou...}

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:13.120
(Right on, right on.)

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.560
I wanna do this, and I wanna do that too. {are mo shitai...}

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:17.500
Let's go!  (Go!!)  {iku...}

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.540
Move out! (Yeah!!) {susu...}

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:20.780
Let's do it with gusto! {gachinko de ...}

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:27.410
Because there's only one you in this world, {sekai ni...}

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:34.570
you've gotta make sure you find the things you love. {daisuki...}

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:53.210
Summer vacation is over almost before it began!

00:23:53.210 --> 00:23:56.080
Get pumped and excited! Let's start the new term!

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:58.640
But there's so much work for the Guardians.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:23:59.950
Amu-chan, we have a problem!

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:02.520
Trouble has broken out!

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:04.580
Huh? When I'm this busy?

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:06.580
Tadase-kun and Rima are swamped, too.

00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:09.150
At times like this, just leave it to me, Yaya-tan!

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:10.270
Yeah!

00:24:10.270 --> 00:24:11.500
Next time on Shugo Chara:

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:12.780
A Request for Yaya!

00:24:12.770 --> 00:24:15.060
Do you think those two can handle this?

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:16.110
I'm a little skeptical.

00:24:16.110 --> 00:24:17.220
Indeed.

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:20.100
Yaya, Pepe, you can do it!
